  "hints": [
    "a line is determined by any two points on it - so a natural brute force checks every pair, but you're redoing a lot of work: fix one point and think about what varies",
    "for a fixed point i, every other point j defines a slope from i to j; points that share the same slope from i lie on the same line through i",
    "count how many other points share each slope from i using a hash map, the best line through i has (max count) + 1 points (the +1 is i itself)",
    "represent slope as a reduced fraction (dy/dx divided by their gcd) with a consistent sign convention, not a floating point division, to avoid precision bugs and to treat vertical lines (dx = 0) as their own bucket",
    "repeat for every point as the fixed point and take the global maximum; since all points are guaranteed unique you don't need special handling for duplicate coordinates"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "using floating point slope (dy / dx) directly, which causes precision mismatches for points that are mathematically on the same line",
    "not reducing dx/dy to lowest terms with a consistent sign, so the same true slope ends up in two different hash map buckets",
    "forgetting to special-case dx = 0 (a vertical line), which would otherwise divide by zero",
    "forgetting to add 1 for the fixed point itself when computing the count for a given slope bucket",
    "recomputing the whole thing with O(n^3) nested pair-checking when the O(n^2) per-point slope grouping is both simpler and faster"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array of `points` on the X-Y plane, where `points[i] = [xi, yi]`.\n\n**Return the maximum number of points that all lie on the same straight line.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= points.length <= 300",
      "points[i].length == 2",
      "-10^4 <= x_i, y_i <= 10^4",
      "all points are unique"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "only one point (answer is 1)",
      "only two points (any two points trivially define a line, answer is 2)",
      "a vertical line (all points share the same x coordinate, undefined slope)",
      "a horizontal line (all points share the same y coordinate, slope 0)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
